<title>USA: Merrill names Williamson to head Intl Bank.</title>
<headline>Merrill names Williamson to head Intl Bank.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc said it named Robert Williamson president and chief executive of Merrill Lynch International Bank, its wholly-owned unit that provides foreign exchange currency and options trading services.</p>
<p>In taking the new post, Williamson, who was chief credit officer of the parent company, fills a vacancy that has existed for some time, a spokesman for Merrill said. No replacement has been announced for Williamson's former post.</p>
<p>-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1730</p>
